  "body": "## Summary\n\nAdopts cargo-nextest for the pkgs/id test suite (issue #6378, queue task 14371).\n\ncargo-nextest was already in the dev shell and in every nix check derivation (`pkgs/id/nix-common.nix` lists it in `nativeBuildInputs`, inherited by `pkgs/id/flake.nix`'s `mkCheckWith`), but no test invocation used it. The PR gate already shards the integration suite by test target (test-shard-0..3, #869/#551); this change adds per-test process parallelism inside each shard and a shared nextest config.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `pkgs/id/.config/nextest.toml` (new): fail-fast off, no retries, `test-threads = \"num-cpus\"`, slow-test marking at 60s (no termination), `ci` profile with junit output.\n- `pkgs/id/justfile`: `test-rust`, `test-sandbox`, `test-full`, `test-unit`, `test-native-shell`, `test-integration`, `test-int-sandbox`, `test-verbose`, `test-one` now run `cargo nextest run`. Recipe names/params/deps unchanged.\n- `pkgs/id/scripts/test-shard-sandbox.sh`: shard commands run nextest; the existing 4-way target sharding is unchanged.\n- `pkgs/id/just-recipes.json`: regenerated — it had drifted on main (`planted-bug-check` recipe missing) and the recorded recipe bodies now match the justfile. The machine-specific `source` path was restored to the previously committed value (the drift check projects it out).\n\n## Coverage preservation\n\n- nextest never runs doc tests, so `test-rust` and shard 0 keep an explicit `cargo test --doc` step.\n- The sandbox `serve_tests` skip is reproduced as `-E 'not test(serve_tests)'`.\n- Crash-gate recipes keep `cargo test`: they rely on `--include-ignored` name-filter semantics.\n- No test is deleted or newly skipped.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo nextest run --all-features --lib` in this worktree: **3467 passed, 1 failed, 15 skipped (pre-existing `#[ignore]`)** of 3468 tests in 132s. The one failure, `web::tests::test_load_asset_urls_from_manifest`, is an environment artifact of the local stub `web/dist` (see below): the identical test fails under plain `cargo test` with the same stub, and after building the real web assets (`bun install` + `bun run build`, as the nix checks do) all 9 `web::tests` pass under nextest, including that test. Oracle: the full pkgs/id lib suite under the new runner, with any failure reproduced under the old runner before it counts as a regression.\n- Filter syntax (`not test(serve_tests)`, `test(name)`) verified on a probe crate against nextest 0.9.146 before use; the committed `.config/nextest.toml` (including the `ci` profile) parses and runs there.\n- `bash scripts/just-recipes-check.sh`: passes (failed on clean main before this change due to the pre-existing drift above).\n- `bash -n scripts/test-shard-sandbox.sh`: OK.\n- Pre-existing, unrelated: a bare `cargo test --all-features --lib` outside the nix shell fails on this tree (and on clean main) because `--all-features` enables the `web` feature whose RustEmbed `web/dist` folder is a bun build artifact; the nix check derivations build it first (`(cd web && bun run build)` in `mkCheckWith`). A stub `web/dist/index.html` (gitignored) was used for the first local nextest run above; the real assets were then built locally to disposition the one stub-caused failure (see the verification bullet).\n\nRefs #6378\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796813050&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8032&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8032&signature=3c10701ea89f1b73d14cafc72ab55675687b96a8c11bb1b98936935ad227857f\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8032?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
